module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: unify_generics folds a call's actuals onto one accumulator and its already-bound arm is `if map_has(acc.subst, g) { acc }` — when a parameter already carries a binding, the later actual is DISCARDED and nothing is said, so a call whose arguments instantiate the same formal type variable to two different types is ACCEPTED on the first binding alone. The caller then receives a declared return type instantiated with a binding that no argument of the call implies. This is a fail-open: the compiler knows the two actuals disagree, prints nothing, and keeps typing the call as if the first one were the whole story (DESIGN section 5, an error must not masquerade as success).",

    "THE SAME SHAPE HID THE DEFECT THAT MADE IT MEASURABLE. The producer repair in the #14152 lane (src/v1/04_infer.dag call arm, commit 81824abfa3) is what first produced a corpus whose Map-returning generic calls disagree about K and V: before it, 39 of the 46 Map-family rebinds compared a call's type against the callee's OWN formal parameters, because an argument-less generic call left the instantiation map empty and `substitute_generics_apply` short-circuits on an empty map, handing the declaration's own K/V to the caller as if instantiated. Those 39 were invisible to this class precisely because the fold was silent: one silent defect was masking another.",

    "MEASUREMENT (2026-10-19, #14152 lane, head 6bd8bd788ce against origin/main 0316e966140, both emitted closures, fresh clones at printed SHAs). Reporting the conflict turns main's silence into 43 self-host and 45 v2-native-cli hard type mismatches across 13 and 12 modules, where main produces 0 in both. Triage by the rendering of the stored binding (instrument triage_conflicts_14152.py, verdicts in triage_self_host.json / triage_v2_native_cli.json beside the logs): 13 genuine disagreements — the class this row files; 19 where the binding being rebound renders as a known fabricated placeholder (Product(Unit<>), an empty Primitive()), which blames the call site for an upstream fabrication and belongs to gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.error_type_fabricated_as_a_type_by_total_accessors rather than here; 11 where the expected and got sides render IDENTICALLY, so the reader sees “expected X, got X” and cannot tell a deliberate refusal apart from a broken comparator. These counts are bounded to that run and that head.",

    "CONSEQUENCE FOR A BUILD, MEASURED NOT INFERRED: these are SeverityError with disposition GateBlocking, and a hard diagnostic stops emission — `V2-NATIVE REFUSAL cause=EmissionRefused stage=emit — compile of src/v2/compiler/source_root_eval.dag [rust]`, head emitted=0 where main emits its 2 seed modules. So a corpus containing such a call cannot be built while the conflict is reported, and the first repair is NOT to soften the report: main's green build is green BECAUSE of the fail-open, and any fix must remove the disagreement rather than its visibility.",

    "REPAIR STATUS, stated against the commit that carries this row rather than against the lane. NOT YET ON MAIN: the report itself -- `UnifyGenericsAcc { subst, diagnostics }`, which turns the already-bound arm into a decision and emits the conflict-path diagnostic, with the RED `generic_type_variable_rebind_conflict_is_reported_when_a_bound_variable_gets_a_different_type` and an arm-naming mutation control. It is deliberately NOT in this change: reporting the conflict makes the corpus refuse emission (measured: 43 self-host and 45 v2-native hard type mismatches where main has 0, head emitted=0 against main's 2 emitted seed modules), so a PR carrying both the report and the producer repair can only be green by softening the report. What THIS change carries is the PRODUCER repair -- fresh per-call-site ids at the ExprCall call arm, `fresh_call_variables` -- whose discriminator is `minted_variables_are_fresh_per_call_site` (PASS on it, FAIL rc=101 on a name-keyed mutant), which needs no conflict reporting to discriminate. So the row is filed with the repair that is provable green, and the report follows as its own change once the corpus clears under it; the conflict-path diagnostic named above is that change's RED, and the 76-diagnostic EmissionRefused at src/v2/compiler/source_root_eval.dag is its gate. NOT PLANNED AS PART OF EITHER: the refine-don't-fix rule (an uninformative binding -- a TypeVariable, or a Product(Unit<>) placeholder -- REFINED by an informative one instead of fixing the slot). 19 of 43 rows satisfy the pre-registered predicate for building it, but the two upstream classes named above (fabricated placeholders, identical renderings) are its prerequisites, and it must be measured against a baseline that can already see the conflict -- so after the report, not beside it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: the type-unification authority (a total fold that drops information and reports nothing). CEILING: the fold's already-bound arm becomes a decision — refine, refuse, or keep — and each choice needs its own control, so the ceiling is reached once the report exists and is not exceeded by softening it. NOT SCHEDULED, AS A BOUNDED OPERATOR DECISION: the disposition of the 19 fabrication-blaming rows and the 11 identical-rendering rows; the decision is scoped to this lane. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the refine-don't-fix rule shared by unify_generics and unify_lambda_solves, admitted once the report is on main, so that a rule change can be measured against a baseline that can already see the conflict.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
